// Music for Aliens
// → 780  
// → Music Theory / Composition
// for a Perpetual Universe
// beyond time, beyond space, beyond human hands
// for those who listen with more than ears

type: graphical_score / conceptual_notation
tempo_vars: mysterioso=72, irregularly=138
dynamics: ppp, mp, pp, pppp, mf, f, fff
articulations: sotto_voce, molto_espressivo, gliss, 8va, come_un_sogno
spatial_marks: spiral_galaxies, radiating_beams, crossed_staves, note_clusters
theme: perpetual / extraterrestrial / non-performable_by_human_hands

SECTION 1  mysterioso  3/4  ppp
  rising dense cluster -> high arch -> large note-spiral  fff
  (galaxy-like coil of 32nd notes)

SECTION 2  sotto voce  4/4  mp
  stacked chords + 8va dashed line
  triangular note-burst
  intersecting beam lattice
  "as if from another galaxy"  pp

SECTION 3  molto espressivo  pp
  undulating glissandi waves
  large inward spiral  "come un sogno"  f
  time sig fragment 15/16

SECTION 4  irregularly  138
  continuous dense chromatic runs
  geometric markers (triangle, square)
  sudden pppp drop + 15/16 bar

SECTION 5  sempre più lontano
  mf ascending beam-fan
  radiating lines across staves
  fading to pp  + lunar-phase glyphs

SECTION 6  finale (or is it?)
  fff massive cluster explosion
  collapsing into final tight spiral
  star glyph

// Listen... and remember... you are not alone.
// pickover.com
